                                            <td class="description">      <br/>
OAuthUtils.handleException(MessageContext mc, Exception e, int status)<br/>
<br/>
causes an IllegalArgumentException when one of the token parameters is invalid, making the oauth request return a 400. However OAuthUtils wants to always throw a NotAuthorizedException, hiding the original error in an IllegalArgumentException (which would better be an IllegalStateException in the first place):<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
