                <tr id="issuerow12657730" rel="12657730" data-issuekey="CXF-5129" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-5129" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-5129">CXF-5129</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Content type is always &quot;text/xml&quot; in case of using @Context HttpServletResponse response
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Sergey Beryozkin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Sergei Malafeev
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Sergei Malafeev
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 15/Jul/13 15:11 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 14/Aug/13 15:49 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 15/Jul/13 20:24 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.7.5            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.7.6,                     3.0.0-milestone1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      In case of next endpoint with @Context HttpServletResponse:<br/>
<br/>
{code}<br/>
@GET<br/>
@Path(&quot;test&quot;)<br/>
@Produces(MediaType.TEXT_PLAIN)<br/>
public void test(@Context HttpServletResponse response) throws IOException {<br/>
       response.setContentType(MediaType.TEXT_PLAIN);<br/>
       response.getOutputStream().print(&quot;test&quot;);<br/>
} <br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
Content-Type in received message is always &quot;text/xml&quot;:<br/>
{code}<br/>
[bash]$ curl &quot;http://localhost:8030/test&quot; -D -<br/>
HTTP/1.1 200 OK<br/>
Content-Type: text/xml;charset=UTF-8<br/>
Content-Length: 4<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
So it is impossible to change Content-Type when @Context is used.<br/>
response.setContentType(MediaType.TEXT_PLAIN) doesn&#39;t work as well as @Produces(MediaType.TEXT_PLAIN)
  </td>
