                <tr id="issuerow12658118" rel="12658118" data-issuekey="CXF-5133" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-5133" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-5133">CXF-5133</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                CXF STS renewed token not itself renewable.
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Colm O hEigeartaigh
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Ethan Wallwork
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Ethan Wallwork
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 16/Jul/13 21:30 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 14/Aug/13 15:49 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 17/Jul/13 13:59 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.7.5            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.7.6,                     2.6.10            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        STS            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Windows XP, Java 1.7
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      When renewing a security token (a SAML assertion in my test case) the returned token cannot be renewed again (nor can the original).  This is true even if the &lt;Renewing/&gt; element is present in the renewal RST message.<br/>
<br/>
It seems that the SAMLTokenRenewer class does not put the STSConstants.TOKEN_RENEWING_ALLOW and STSConstants.TOKEN_RENEWING_ALLOW_AFTER_EXPIRY properties on the SecurityTOken placed in the token store, which are required for renewal to later take place.<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
