                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I&#39;m using SearchContext in conjunction with SearchBean to extract search parameters from the _s query parameter. Unfortunately there seems to be a parsing issue, because providing a search query like<br/>
<br/>
?_s=name==CXF<br/>
<br/>
and visitor implementation like this<br/>
<br/>
            @Override<br/>
            public void visit(SearchCondition&lt;SearchBean&gt; sc) {<br/>
                PrimitiveStatement p = sc.getStatement();<br/>
                if (p != null) {<br/>
                    LOGGER.error(&quot;{} {} {}&quot;, p.getProperty(), p.getCondition(), p.getValue());<br/>
                }<br/>
            }<br/>
<br/>
will log<br/>
<br/>
name EQUALS CXF?=
  </td>
