</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">3</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      The JAASAuthenticationFilter not rfc2617 compliant for WWW-Authenticate realms.  Currently the returned headers for a realm called &quot;foo&quot; would return:<br/>
<br/>
Basic foo<br/>
<br/>
However, according to rfc2617 p2/3 it states: <br/>
<br/>
The authentication parameter realm is defined for all authentication<br/>
   schemes:<br/>
      realm       = &quot;realm&quot; &quot;=&quot; realm-value<br/>
      realm-value = quoted-string<br/>
<br/>
Therefor the above example is supposed to look like the following:<br/>
<br/>
Basic realm=&quot;foo&quot;<br/>
<br/>
This will make the JAX-RS authentication compliant with the rfc and also compatible with other implementations such as Jetty.<br/>

  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
