                <tr id="issuerow12666155" rel="12666155" data-issuekey="CXF-5242" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-5242" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-5242">CXF-5242</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                JMS Topic based replies can lose messages
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 29/Aug/13 16:27 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 27/Sep/13 18:18 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 29/Aug/13 19:10 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.6.9,                     2.7.6            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.6.10,                     2.7.7            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Transports            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      <br/>
If you use a Topic for a JMS reply queue (not sure why you would, likely a bad practice) for a request/reply interaction, there is a very small period of time between when the message is sent and the listener starts listening.   If the server responds in that time period, the response is lost as there is no listener on the topic.<br/>

  </td>
