                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      As I understand, it wasn&#39;t possible to update headers inside JAX-RS 2.0 ContainerRequestFilter. <br/>
Is was fixed in this issue https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-4986.<br/>
<br/>
But now update of Content-Type header inside of @PreMatching filter doesn&#39;t affect further processing - <br/>
suitable MessageBodyReader is selected using initial Content-Type but not new one.  <br/>

  </td>
