                <tr id="issuerow12668012" rel="12668012" data-issuekey="CXF-5270" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-5270" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-5270">CXF-5270</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                XKMS Crypto Client does not check local keystore for &quot;locate&quot; if the alias is actually a Subject DN
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Colm O hEigeartaigh
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Colm O hEigeartaigh
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Colm O hEigeartaigh
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 11/Sep/13 09:50 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 27/Sep/13 18:18 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 11/Sep/13 10:54 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.7.7            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Services            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      <br/>
The XKMS Crypto provider tries to get a Certificate for the value configured for &quot;ws-security.encryption.username&quot;. WSS4J treats this as an &quot;alias&quot;, and the XKMS Crypto Provider first tries to get the Certificate from a local keystore using this, before going off to the XKMS Server. However, if the encryption username is in the form of a Subject DN it will fail to retrieve the certificate locally, and always call out to the XKMS Server.
  </td>
