                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Currently XKMS validate() operation checks only validity period, trusted chain and CRLs of X509 certificate. Basically it is not necessary that certificate exists in the XKMS repository.<br/>
However, in some cases it is required that certificate itself is &quot;known&quot; by XKMS (direct trust).<br/>
For such cases XKMS validation request should additionally contain element &lt;KeyUsage&gt;http://www.w3.org/2002/03/xkms#Signature&lt;/KeyUsage&gt;. This element triggers direct trust validation.
  </td>
