                <tr id="issuerow12695736" rel="12695736" data-issuekey="CXF-5569" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-5569" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-5569">CXF-5569</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                OAuth AbstractAuthFilter and query parameters used for signing
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Sergey Beryozkin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Jason Klapste
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Jason Klapste
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 18/Feb/14 17:25 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 11/Jul/14 12:50 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 19/Feb/14 17:38 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.7.10            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        3.0.0-milestone2,                     2.7.11            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-RS Security            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      In the AbstractAuthFilter the query (or body) parameters used for signing are only those included in ALLOWED_OAUTH_PARAMETERS.<br/>
<br/>
But if I&#39;m reading the RFC correctly, it looks are though ALL parameters should be considered for signature generation.<br/>
<br/>
To support both backwards compatibility, can I suggest exposing the ALLOWED_OAUTH_PARAMETERS to subclasses (either directly or via getter/setters) along with a flag that can be set to automatically include any and all parameters?
  </td>
