</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                                        CXF-2911                        </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      When using Apache CXF (through JBossWS integration) on top of JBoss AS 7 (whose web layer is based on JBoss Web, basically a fork of Tomcat), I&#39;m still seeing the defect previously dealt with in https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-2911 . This time, however, the MEP is not oneway, but a request-response one with WS-Addressing enabled and the ReplyTo header property specified to a non generic address.<br/>
The net effect is that a HTTP 202 response is immediately dispatched to the caller, letting Tomcat recycle the underlying httpservlet request.
  </td>
