java.lang.ClassCastException: java.net.URI cannot be cast to java.lang.String<br/>
<br/>
<br/>
Test:<br/>
{code}<br/>
 Response response = getWebClient()<br/>
                .path(&quot;/blob&quot;)<br/>
                .type(MediaType.MULTIPART_FORM_DATA)<br/>
                .post(multipartBody);<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
serverside resource:<br/>
{code}<br/>
        URI blobId = UriBuilder.fromResource(getClass()).build(gridFSDBFile.getId());<br/>
        return Response.created(blobId).build();<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
because inside WebClient handleResponse -&gt; AbstractClient the values are assumed to be string arrays, but is an URI object:<br/>
{code}<br/>
