                <tr id="issuerow12707912" rel="12707912" data-issuekey="CXF-5685" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-5685" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-5685">CXF-5685</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Extended support for wsdl11external WS-PolicyAttachments references
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Andrei Shakirin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Andrei Shakirin
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Andrei Shakirin
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 11/Apr/14 10:49 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 11/Jul/14 12:51 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 28/Apr/14 09:42 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        3.0.0-milestone2,                     2.7.10            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        3.0,                     2.7.12            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-WS Runtime            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Currently CXF supports only limited set of references for external WS-PolicyAttachments (wsa:EndpointReferenceType):<br/>
<br/>
&lt;attachments xmlns:wsp=&quot;http://www.w3.org/ns/ws-policy&quot; xmlns:test=&quot;http://x.y.z/Assertions&quot;&gt;<br/>
    &lt;wsp:PolicyAttachment&gt;<br/>
        &lt;wsp:AppliesTo&gt;<br/>
            &lt;wsa:EndpointReferenceType xmlns:wsa=&quot;http://www.w3.org/2005/08/addressing&quot;&gt;<br/>
                &lt;wsa:Address&gt;http://x.y.z/GreeterPort&lt;/wsa:Address&gt;<br/>
            &lt;/wsa:EndpointReferenceType&gt;<br/>
        &lt;/wsp:AppliesTo&gt;<br/>
        &lt;wsp:Policy&gt;<br/>
           &lt;test:A&gt;A&lt;/test:A&gt;<br/>
        &lt;/wsp:Policy&gt;<br/>
    &lt;/wsp:PolicyAttachment&gt;    <br/>
&lt;/attachments&gt;<br/>
<br/>
I propose to extend that to support at least some URI Domain Expression for wsdl11:<br/>
wsdl11.definitions() <br/>
wsdl11.service(service) <br/>
wsdl11.binding(binding)<br/>
wsdl11.bindingOperation(binding/operation)<br/>
wsdl11.bindingOperation.input(binding/operation)<br/>
wsdl11.bindingOperation.output(binding/operation)<br/>
wsdl11.bindingOperation.fault(binding/operation/fault)<br/>

  </td>
