                <tr id="issuerow12709016" rel="12709016" data-issuekey="CXF-5698" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-5698" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-5698">CXF-5698</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Use the service root path instead of the initial request path to restrict websocket service access
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Open
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    <em>Unresolved</em>
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Akitoshi Yoshida
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Akitoshi Yoshida
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Akitoshi Yoshida
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 17/Apr/14 09:44 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 14/May/14 10:37 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        Transports            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Currently, the URL path used to initiate the websocket connection is used to allow or restrict the subsequent operations received over the websocket.<br/>
<br/>
This is not convenient as the caller must know the service root path to be able to invoke all the operations supported by the service. A more convenient approach would be to use the service root path as the filter so that the subsequent requests to one of its operations can be processed even if the initial connection request uses one of these sub resource paths.<br/>
<br/>

  </td>
