                <tr id="issuerow12728886" rel="12728886" data-issuekey="CXF-5896" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-5896" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-5896">CXF-5896</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Limiting upload size with &quot;attachment-max-size&quot; or &quot;org.apache.cxf.io.CachedOutputStream.MaxSize&quot; not working
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Not A Problem
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Daniel Kulp
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Abel Salgado Romero
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Abel Salgado Romero
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 22/Jul/14 16:05 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 16/Feb/15 16:31 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 22/Jul/14 19:03 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        Invalid            </td>
                                            <td class="components">                        WS-* Components            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment">      Tomcat 6, CXF 2.7.3
  </td>
                                            <td class="description">      Hi,<br/>
<br/>
I’m using a WebService with MTOM and Base64 for file transfer and everything works fine. However I received the requirement to limit the size of the file uploaded at a framework level avoid any OutOfMemory error before the files are fully transferred to the client.<br/>
So far, these errors only happen when using the Base64, files bigger than 30 MB, but we want to limit the size no matter the protocol (MTOM or Base64).<br/>
Searching for information the only thing found has been this http://cxf.apache.org/docs/jax-rs-multiparts.html, however it not very clear in its use or if the values are set in KB, bytes, etc.<br/>
Anyway I have configured out WebService setting the properties but they seem to be ignored, I have tried also setting the system properties…and nothing happens.<br/>
Here is what I tried in my endpoint configuration.<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
&lt;jaxws:endpoint id=&quot;service&quot; implementor=&quot;#serviceImpl&quot;<br/>
		address=&quot;/ServiceLocation&quot;<br/>
		&lt;jaxws:properties&gt;<br/>
			&lt;entry key=&quot;attachment-directory&quot; value=&quot;c:/cxf/uploads&quot; /&gt;<br/>
			&lt;entry key=&quot;attachment-memory-threshold&quot; value=&quot;10&quot; /&gt;<br/>
			&lt;entry key=&quot;attachment-max-size&quot; value=&quot;10&quot; /&gt;<br/>
		&lt;/jaxws:properties&gt;<br/>
	&lt;/jaxws:endpoint&gt;<br/>
{noformat}<br/>
I noted that the documentation states “jaxrs:properties”, ¿does this only work for Jax-RS?<br/>

  </td>
