                <tr id="issuerow12733413" rel="12733413" data-issuekey="CXF-5939" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-5939" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-5939">CXF-5939</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                Support mtom configuration at run time using Accept header
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Improvement</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Minor
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Invalid
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Jason Pell
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Jason Pell
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Jason Pell
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 12/Aug/14 08:08 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 13/Aug/14 03:16 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 13/Aug/14 03:16 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        2.7.12,                     3.0.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="components">                        JAX-WS Runtime            </td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">1</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      If the Accept header is empty, and mtom is enabled, mtom will function as before.  <br/>
<br/>
If any Accept headers are defined, then In order for MTOM to be enabled, the header must be one of:<br/>
<br/>
1) *<br/>
2) */*<br/>
3) application/*<br/>
4) application/xop+xml<br/>
<br/>
Any other headers will cause the attachments to be inlined.  Existing MTOM thresholds, etc will continue to be effective.<br/>
<br/>
I noted this very old discussion on the topic<br/>
https://www.java.net/node/686289<br/>

  </td>
                                            <td class="security"></td>
                                            <td class="progress">     
</td>
