                <tr id="issuerow12740347" rel="12740347" data-issuekey="CXF-5995" class="issuerow">
                                            <td class="project">    CXF
</td>
                                            <td class="issuekey">

    <a class="issue-link" data-issue-key="CXF-5995" href="https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/CXF-5995">CXF-5995</a>
</td>
                                            <td class="summary"><p>
                ClientProxyImpl problem with handling @BeanParams with null headers/cookies.
    </p>
</td>
                                            <td class="issuetype"> Bug</td>
                                            <td class="status">
                Closed
    </td>
                                            <td class="priority">   Major
</td>
                                            <td class="resolution">    Fixed
</td>
                                            <td class="assignee">            Sergey Beryozkin
    </td>
                                            <td class="reporter">            Michał P
    </td>
                                            <td class="creator">            Michał P
    </td>
                                            <td class="created"> 10/Sep/14 09:03 </td>
                                            <td class="lastViewed"> &nbsp; </td>
                                            <td class="updated"> 16/Feb/15 16:09 </td>
                                            <td class="resolutiondate"> 10/Sep/14 10:40 </td>
                                            <td class="versions">                        3.0,                     3.0.1            </td>
                                            <td class="fixVersions">                        2.7.13,                     3.0.2,                     3.1            </td>
                                            <td class="components">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="duedate">    &nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="votes">0</td>
                                            <td class="watches">2</td>
                                            <td class="thumbnail"></td>
                                            <td class="timeoriginalestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Problem occures when my @BeanParam object has String @HeaderParam values that are null.<br/>
<br/>
On client side inside ClientProxyImpl#getValuesFromBeanParam always returns full Map&lt;String, BeanPair&gt; even when BeanPair has null values.<br/>
<br/>
{code:title=ClientProxyImpl.java|borderStyle=solid}<br/>
// line 481<br/>
String propertyName = m.getName().substring(3);<br/>
Method getter = bean.getClass().getMethod(&quot;get&quot; + propertyName, new Class[]{});<br/>
// Object value is null<br/>
Object value = getter.invoke(bean, new Object[]{});<br/>
String annotationValue = AnnotationUtils.getAnnotationValue(annotation);<br/>
values.put(annotationValue, new BeanPair(value, m.getParameterAnnotations()[0]));<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
Methods such handleHeaders, handleCookies has useless condition that is<br/>
always true (BeanPair is never null)<br/>
<br/>
{code:title=ClientProxyImpl.java|borderStyle=solid}<br/>
// line 585<br/>
for (Map.Entry&lt;String, BeanPair&gt; entry : values.entrySet()) {<br/>
    if (entry.getValue() != null) {<br/>
        headers.add(entry.getKey(), convertParamValue(entry.getValue().getValue(), entry.getValue().getAnns()));<br/>
    }<br/>
}<br/>
{code}<br/>
<br/>
That couses unintended behaviour on server side when server receives BeanParam objects with fields with String value equal to &quot;null&quot;.<br/>
<br/>
I&#39;ve sent no headers but servers received header with &quot;null&quot; String.
