                                            <td class="timeestimate"></td>
                                            <td class="timespent"></td>
                                            <td class="workratio">&nbsp;
</td>
                                            <td class="subtasks">                </td>
                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      I am considering using Apache CXF in Cloud environments (Azure, AWS and others).   The CXF web service will be used with a load-balancer.   I need to measure the capacity of a single CXF endpoint, which brings me to ask these important questions: Is a CXF endpoint multi-thread capable?    Assuming that the answer is YES, is there a way to adjust the number of threads?    I don&#39;t see any section of the CXF documentation that talks about this topic.   I think that this topic is important enough to have a section in the documentation for it.
  </td>
