                                            <td class="issuelinks">                </td>
                                            <td class="environment"></td>
                                            <td class="description">      Hi<br/>
<br/>
tested on last 2.6 release and didn&#39;t take time to check on 3. but I guess it is the same:<br/>
<br/>
I call a rest endpoint, in my business I login(user, pass) from the request (http) then from the security context I get the principal -&gt; null, if I get it fro mthe request it is avlued. It is cause org.apache.cxf.transport.http.AbstractHTTPDestination#setupMessage(org.apache.cxf.message.Message, javax.servlet.ServletConfig, javax.servlet.ServletContext, javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest, javax.servlet.http.HttpServletResponse) stores the principal for the request but it evaluates it too early.<br/>
<br/>
Why not keeping the delegation to the http request?
